      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What to Check After High Winds in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Shingles: Look for missing, torn, creased, or unsealed shingles (even if they lie flat again, broken adhesive seals can let moisture in).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Flashing & Vents: Check around chimneys, roof valleys, and vents for lifted metal or loose seals.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Debris & Leaks: Watch for punctures from branches or flying debris, and check ceilings or attics for early signs of water intrusion. If rain or snow is forecast, get temporary tarping before permanent repairs.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              6,
              7
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
